          "generated_prob": 0.0009104378363525179,
          "sentence": "To demonstrate this, he has readers and listeners put imaginary words into the past participle, namely a two-syllable word such as “quaffen” and a three-syllable word ending in “-ieren,” such as “flagieren.” He then claims that the result, “gequafft” and “flagiert,” means that words ending in “-ieren” form an exception.",
